Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:12:24 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Refuse EXPLAIN COSTS on tables under a row access or
 masking policy

EXPLAIN COSTS prints the optimizer's column statistics of every table a
statement reads: minimum, maximum, null fraction and distinct count over
all rows. A row access policy does not narrow them, so a user under a row
filter read the range and cardinality of the rows it hides (measured on
4.1.7: a user allowed ids 1 and 3 of an Iceberg table saw id [1.0, 4.0]).

EXPLAIN COSTS is now refused with error 5213 when a row access or column
masking policy applies to the user on any table the statement reads,
through views and CTEs too. The other EXPLAIN levels print no column
statistics and stay allowed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
